## 6. Integration with the Manufacturing Model

The MRP configuration was developed using the production engineering data previously calculated in Microsoft Excel.

The relationship between the engineering model and SAP planning parameters included:

| Engineering Input | SAP Planning Application |
|---|---|
| Annual production requirements | Demand and production planning |
| Production lot dimensioning | Lot-sizing parameters |
| Material consumption calculations | Material requirements planning |
| Supplier lead times | Procurement planning |
| Reorder point calculations | MRP parameters for raw materials |
| Manufacturing routings | Production scheduling |
| Material classification | Material Master and Material Groups |
| Inventory organization | Storage Locations |

This integration illustrates how engineering calculations can be translated into structured ERP planning parameters.

## 7. Conclusion

The PHOS project adopted a Make-to-Stock production strategy supported by differentiated MRP and lot-sizing procedures.

Manual reorder point planning with fixed lot sizes was selected for raw materials, while deterministic MRP with lot-for-lot sizing was adopted for semi-finished and finished products.

The planning configuration was supported by production capacity analysis, supplier lead-time evaluation, material requirements calculations, and SAP organizational data.

This phase demonstrates the connection between industrial engineering decisions and their application within SAP S/4HANA Production Planning and Materials Management.
